{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":503079,"name":"Jason Chollar","username":"Jason_Chollar","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/cc9497/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-28T21:20:47.880Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503079-feature-request-for-productservice-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503079-feature-request-for-productservice-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFeature request for product/service\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e– Other –\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503079-describe-the-request-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503079-describe-the-request-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the request\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’d love a built-in way, like a first-party Grok Bot connector, for my bots to read my own usage: how much of my weekly allowance is left, and how much on-demand I’ve used.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy: last weekend I ran several research bots at once and burned through my whole weekly allowance, then $8 of my $10 on-demand cushion, with no warning. Right now the only view is the Usage page in Settings, and the bots can’t see it at all.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat would help:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBots can report my remaining allowance when I ask.\u003cbr\u003e\nBefore a big job like deep research, a bot gives a rough estimate (“this will likely use about 20% of what’s left”) so I can decide first.\u003cbr\u003e\nAn optional warning when I’m close to spilling into on-demand.\u003cbr\u003e\nRelated: Weekly usage spills into On-Demand with no warning\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnyone else want this?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-28T21:20:53.670Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":25.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":173270,"topic_slug":"feature-request-let-grok-bot-see-its-own-usage-stats","display_username":"